      "strings": {
        "brief": "You're on an authorised exercise at Carrholme Services, a fictional firm. You are covering the Care Laundry desk this morning, clearing the queue. First you make some of the ordinary choices anyone would make on a busy morning; then you see, six months on, where each one led. Then you take the desk's inbox one item at a time. Only the inbox is scored.",
        "flipHeading": "Six months later",
        "defendIntro": "Take the Care Laundry desk inbox one item at a time and decide what to do with each. Anything about someone's personal data, a request to see, correct or delete it, or a breach, goes to the DPO the same day; report or check anything that doesn't sit right. There's no clock on you here.",
        "mondayCard": "If personal data goes somewhere it should not, or someone asks to see, correct or delete their data, or complains about how we used it, tell your DPO the same day. Do not wait to be sure, and do not try to fix it alone.",
        "noBlameLine": "Mistakes with personal data happen to careful people, usually when they are busy. What turns a mistake into harm is silence. Nobody at Carrholme is in trouble for reporting, including their own slip.",
        "defendOnly": "Any of these can catch a careful person on a busy morning. The ones you were caught out by are shown below, with what good looks like. Reporting fast is what limits the harm.",
        "conceptPanel": {
          "heading": "Behind every row is a person",
          "text": "Behind every row in a spreadsheet is a person. If it goes wrong, tell the DPO straight away."
        },
        "flipMontageByChoice": {
          "overtime_sheet": {
            "send_wrong_sam": "The overtime sheet, with the back-injury and union-meeting notes, sat in a care home manager's inbox for three days before anyone noticed. Three days the DPO never had, to warn the staff and limit the harm.",
            "check_then_send": "The version where it went to the first Sam instead: staff health notes reached someone outside Carrholme, unnoticed for three days. A glance at the address stopped it here."
          },
          "caller_bernadette": {
            "give_details": "Two weeks on, a stranger was waiting for Bernadette outside her school. The birthday-surprise call was how he learned where a lone worker would be, and when.",
            "take_message": "The version where the school and the time were given out: a stranger learned where a lone worker would be. Offering to pass a message gave the caller nothing."
          },
          "marketing_export": {
            "export_list": "A month on, three families complained and one wrote to the regulator. The contacts had been given to sort out a lost cardigan, not to hear about offers.",
            "ask_dpo": "The version where the list was exported: families who had given their details to sort a claim got a marketing email, and complained. Asking first turned it into a proper sign-up box."
          },
          "redaction_send": {
            "send_as_is": "Mr Hale opened the report and read another resident's continence-care note and a driver's mobile number. One mistake, two more people's data exposed.",
            "redact_first": "The version where the report went as it was: another resident's care note and a driver's mobile reached a stranger. Taking the extra details out first left only what Mr Hale was owed."
          }
        }
